<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Andrea Doria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1466–1560</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Andrea Doria was a Genoese admiral and statesman, the leading naval commander of his age. In 1528 he switched from French to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> service, restored <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a>'s independence under a new aristocratic constitution and became its dominant figure for three decades. As admiral of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a> he fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barbary-coast">Barbary</a> corsairs, and he survived the Fieschi conspiracy against him in 1547.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/andrea-doria.jpg" alt="Andrea Doria" width="320" height="465" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sebastiano del Piombo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Andrea_Doria.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
